# Normalize to LF on checkout and in the working tree.
#
# Why this matters here rather than being cosmetic: the plugin's own gates PARSE
# source text. `tools/check-template-literals.mjs` and `test/client-css.mjs` walk
# template strings and CSS, and the build asserts an end marker survives at a
# known position. Autocrlf would rewrite every tracked file on a fresh clone and
# make a Windows checkout differ from CI.
*
text=auto eol=lf

# Images are the one thing that must not be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary

# PowerShell scripts are the exception: Windows tooling copes better with CRLF,
# and these are run by hand on Windows only.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
